  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.1: First release-candidate-preview cut. API surface is stable and expected to ship unchanged in 1.0. Headline capabilities: AddPostQuantumJwtBearer() one-line wireup, fail-closed validation handler, JWKS-equivalent IPostQuantumJwtKeyRing with HTTP-backed implementation + hosted-service warmup, four event hooks (OnMessageReceived / OnTokenValidated / OnAuthenticationFailed / OnChallenge), distributed jti replay protection via the companion PostQuantum.AspNetCore.RedisReplayCache package, first-class observability via System.Diagnostics.Metrics + ActivitySource, AOT-compatible (verified on Linux / Windows / macOS in CI). Documentation: SECURITY-MODEL, GETTING-STARTED, RECIPES (13 scenarios), FAQ, PRODUCTION-CHECKLIST, MIGRATION (from both AddJwtBearer and PostQuantum.Jwt.AspNetCore), DIAGNOSTICS, PERFORMANCE, API-STABILITY. Samples: minimal API, SignalR with in-page client, MVC with controllers + policies. 66 tests, zero skips on PQ-capable hosts. Crypto construction (in the underlying PostQuantum.Jwt engine) is not yet independently audited — see KNOWN-GAPS.md before depending on this. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-aspnetcore/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md.",
